","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-23-2018, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T15:35:05-07:00","id":1210641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1210469#post1210469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I can remove the rote benefit to balance it out? Moving the ability to resist supernatural attempts to learn their names to the Hallowed Name rite could also solve the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does feel like an ability that is not handed out lightly. Tiring it to a rite certainly removes that issue","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T17:22:29-07:00","id":1210690,"title":"","content":"Yeah, could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:17:11-07:00","id":1210797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1210641#post1210641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does feel like an ability that is not handed out lightly. Tiring it to a rite certainly removes that issue</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1210690#post1210690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I've left the tracking spoor benefit and moved the name protection aspect over to the Hallowed Name Rite. How does its writeup look with it?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Hallowed Name</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022, Wolf Rite)</b><br /> The Lodge recognizes the power to be found in knowing one's name, and that people are connected to the wider world by the abstract ties forged over the course of their lives. They also are aware that witches with the right knowledge can exploit those connections to work their magic upon a person, or those close to him. This rite is performed to hinder such tampering.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Connections, True Name, Warding<br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> The ritualist holds an item of significance to the subject and speaks their name. He then chants a warding mantra in the First Tongue, his words slow and steady as the desired enchantment is woven into being. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (10 Successes, each roll represents 1 minute)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Month<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> For the duration of the rite, any attempt to cast sympathetic magic on or through its recipient fails unless she spends a Willpower point, or knows his sympathetic name. Even then, this triggers a Clash of Wills, with the werewolf rolling Resolve + Primal Urge with the 8-again quality. At Storyteller Discretion, the effects can affect not only Awakened spells, but also other forms of ritual magic like Kindred Blood Sorcery, Sin-Eater Ceremonies, and the Rites of other werewolves.<br /> <br /> The Rite also provides protection against sny supernatural attempts made to discover his names. Even Uratha who use the Knowledge Facet, Know Thy Prey, suffer from a strange gap in information that's accompanied by a sense of dread or trespassing. They learn nothing of the names used by him, nor any Alternate Identity and Fame Merits he possesses. They also must make a successful Resolve + Composure roll or suffer the Confused Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T05:00:46-07:00","id":1211368,"title":"","content":"Honestly, that feels like it is at least a 4 dot rite. And it missing a Symbol. I recommend <i><b>Hunger.</b></i> It is the Eater of Names after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T06:31:40-07:00","id":1211389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1211368#post1211368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, that feels like it is at least a 4 dot rite. And it missing a Symbol. I recommend <i><b>Hunger.</b></i> It is the Eater of Names after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. How about the five-dot Feast of Names? Does it work as well for them? I also updated the dot rating and Symbols for Hallowed Name on the main post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-25-2018, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T07:41:20-07:00","id":1211406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1211368#post1211368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, that feels like it is at least a 4 dot rite. And it missing a Symbol. I recommend <i><b>Hunger.</b></i> It is the Eater of Names after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Is there conceptual &quot;room&quot; for a quasi-teleport-like effect that lets a hunting Pack travel <i>along</i> a targets name, like it was some kind of path? I think traditional tracking based on Sympathetic Connections is more in theme, but I just thought I'd throw that out there.<br /> <br /> Other Name-based Rite ideas:<br /> * Empower attacks or other Rite usage against a Named target.<br /> * Defensive version of the above.<br /> * &quot;Borrowing&quot; a Target's identity, like a Demon's Identity Theft Embed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T08:39:13-07:00","id":1211433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1211406#post1211406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Is there conceptual &amp;quot;room&amp;quot; for a quasi-teleport-like effect that lets a hunting Pack travel <i>along</i> a targets name, like it was some kind of path? I think traditional tracking based on Sympathetic Connections is more in theme, but I just thought I'd throw that out there.<br /> <br /> Other Name-based Rite ideas:<br /> * Empower attacks or other Rite usage against a Named target.<br /> * Defensive version of the above.<br /> * &amp;quot;Borrowing&amp;quot; a Target's identity, like a Demon's Identity Theft Embed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the third suggestion a lot. I might have to look up that Embed to see if it'd work, but the Guardians' Masque Merit is also another source of inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:07:06-07:00","id":1213909,"title":"","content":"And finally, a Totem section for the Eater of Names herself. i'll be updating this section periodically.<br /> <br /> -==-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mu'Huhisfuruhasamsa</u></b><br /> <i>Rank 6 Firstborn</i><br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 13*, Finesse 15*, Resistance 10*<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Wolves 3, Names 5**, Secrets 2<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Image, Materialized, Reaching, Royal Avatar, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Camouflage, Counterspell, Emotional Aura, Essence Thief, Hallucinations, Innocuous, Mortal Mask, Pathfinder, Sign, Soul Snatch, Speed, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190223-forsaken-february-heralds-of-the-firstborn?p=1192771#post1192771\">Untraceable</a><br /> <br /> <b>Size:</b> 10<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 26*<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 120**<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10*<br /> <b>Defense: </b>13*<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>31*<br /> <b>Speed: </b>37*<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> The Eater of Names must offer a service to whoever tells her their True Name.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> A weapon marked with the First Tongue glyphs for her True Name.<br /> <br /> * - When struck by her Bane for the first time, the Eater of Names is treated as a Rank 5 spirit with the following Attributes and Traits. If she was injured while in this state, the duration is extended for long as she has damage to her Corpus.<br /> <br /> ** - As a Lodge Totem, the Eater of Names gains two Influence dots and receives 10 Essence per day.<br /> <br /> *** - Owing to its deeper bond with them, Humuz-Ur is completely aware of the location, health and emotional state of all her adherents within 200 yards. Those who have offered their True Names to her (via the Feast of Names Rite) can be tracked anywhere so long as they are in the same plane of existence.<br /> <br /> **** - Whenever she uses the Royal Avatar Manifestation to create a Herald for herself, Mu'Huhisfuruhasamsa commonly bestows upon it the Claim, Gauntlet Breach, Materialized, and/or Possess Manifestations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-06-2018, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:28:31-07:00","id":1213918,"title":"","content":"Rank 5 puts her in range of Mage Spirit control, though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:32:35-07:00","id":1213920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1213918#post1213918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 5 puts her in range of Mage Spirit control, though...</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming our hypothetical mage can even get to the god in person, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T16:19:57-07:00","id":1213947,"title":"","content":"It is a bit of a glaring weakness especially for something that hunts mages and promotes the hunting of them.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't want to add blanket immunity to things you could add Countermagic as a Numen. 'The spirit can reflexively countermagic any form of magic, including covert spells. Spend one Essence and roll Power + Finesse. If successes rolled for the spirit meet or exceed those for the spell, the spell is countered.'<br /> <br /> It should probably have higher Influence in Names, too. The Thief of Names is the same Rank and has 5 and doesn't have a cult following.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling you aim for more low-power games, is that accurate Deionscribe? I know some people don't like having Rank 6 or higher things in their settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-01-2018, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T16:27:01-07:00","id":1213953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1213947#post1213947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a bit of a glaring weakness especially for something that hunts mages and promotes the hunting of them.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't want to add blanket immunity to things you could add Countermagic as a Numen. 'The spirit can reflexively countermagic any form of magic, including covert spells. Spend one Essence and roll Power + Finesse. If successes rolled for the spirit meet or exceed those for the spell, the spell is countered.'<br /> <br /> It should probably have higher Influence in Names, too. The Thief of Names is the same Rank and has 5 and doesn't have a cult following.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling you aim for more low-power games, is that accurate Deionscribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the Counterspell Numen. It\u2019s my favorite Numen for Mage. Seriously, it should\u2019ve been in Mage 2E core - that alone could\u2019ve dispelled much of the notion that mages can trample around spirits without fear of reprisal. (Well, Adepts and Masters of Spirit usually can, but still)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T01:21:38-07:00","id":1214080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1213947#post1213947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a bit of a glaring weakness especially for something that hunts mages and promotes the hunting of them.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't want to add blanket immunity to things you could add Countermagic as a Numen. 'The spirit can reflexively countermagic any form of magic, including covert spells. Spend one Essence and roll Power + Finesse. If successes rolled for the spirit meet or exceed those for the spell, the spell is countered.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of swapping out Aggressive Meme for Counterspell since it seemed more appropriate. If you pair that with the Untraceable Numen from Acro's Knight of the Crossroads, then it's almost impossible for most Mages to fight through sympathetic magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It should probably have higher Influence in Names, too. The Thief of Names is the same Rank and has 5 and doesn't have a cult following.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling you aim for more low-power games, is that accurate Deionscribe? I know some people don't like having Rank 6 or higher things in their settings. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I ought to take out Speed and/or Mortal Mask for more Influence dots? Alternatively, I could make the Nameless Wolves match the Tribal Pillars in influence (as they recruit from Forsaken, Pure, and Ghost Wolves) to give it that extra Influence dot alongside extra Essence.<br /> <br /> As for your question of low-power games, the reason I aimed for making the Eater of Names a Rank 5 being was for story purposes. Sure, she's a Firstborn, but perhaps having no Tribe and being forgotten for the most part makes her weaker than the likes of the Tribal Totems and also puts her in a position like Isim-Ur of the Eaters of the Dead.<br /> <br /> .... Now that I think about it, though, this disparity in power ought to be explored in a plot hook for the Lodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T01:25:24-07:00","id":1214081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1213920#post1213920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming our hypothetical mage can even get to the god in person, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>And avoid getting their soul snatched. But even then, having the Untraceable Numen already makes going after her very difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1213953#post1213953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, the Counterspell Numen. It\u2019s my favorite Numen for Mage. Seriously, it should\u2019ve been in Mage 2E core - that alone could\u2019ve dispelled much of the notion that mages can trample around spirits without fear of reprisal. (Well, Adepts and Masters of Spirit usually can, but still)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. It did deserve more than a small sidebar in &quot;To the Strongest&quot;. On a semi-related note, I am thinking of swapping out one of the Numina I placed for Counterspell. Should it be Aggressive Meme, Speed, or Mortal Mask that I should take out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T03:34:46-07:00","id":1214093,"title":"","content":"Removing a Numen... tough choice. I\u2019d get rid of Aggressive Meme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T06:21:58-07:00","id":1214127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1214093#post1214093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Removing a Numen... tough choice. I\u2019d get rid of Aggressive Meme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Done.<br /> <br /> I've also added an extra Influence dot and raised the Essence the Eater of Names receives as a Lodge Totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T16:39:56-07:00","id":1214829,"title":"","content":"Aside from giving myself another reason to post my ephemeral being house rules, I've updated Mu'Huhisfuruhasamsa as a Rank 6 Totem with some sidenotes for how to possibly handle a combat scene with her. The gist of it is that you need to have her Bane on hand to even consider fighting her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T19:11:07-07:00","id":1214877,"title":"","content":"Using bans and banes to bring down a Rank 6+ entity\u2019s traits to that of a Rank 5? That\u2019s a nice idea. I see it as fulfilling both the \u201cthe gods proper shouldn\u2019t be statted up\u201d and \u201cwe still need some concrete way to interact with them\u201d arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T06:51:46-07:00","id":1215021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1214877#post1214877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using bans and banes to bring down a Rank 6+ entity\u2019s traits to that of a Rank 5? That\u2019s a nice idea. I see it as fulfilling both the \u201cthe gods proper shouldn\u2019t be statted up\u201d and \u201cwe still need some concrete way to interact with them\u201d arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly does, although I still need to work out the duration of this effect. Does a scene work as a minmum if it's not struck at least a second time to deal actual damage? While aggravated damage from the Bane prolongs it so long as it's not healed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:24:21-07:00","id":1215033,"title":"","content":"Sounds reasonable. At first I thought only of a single scene... but that makes it way too easy for the god to just run away, recuperate, and strike back. <br /> <br /> This all ties into that set of house rules you mentioned, I presume?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:32:43-07:00","id":1215106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/930317-the-eaters-of-names-2e-homebrew?p=1215033#post1215033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds reasonable. At first I thought only of a single scene... but that makes it way too easy for the god to just run away, recuperate, and strike back. <br /> <br /> This all ties into that set of house rules you mentioned, I presume?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. I'll be free for the weekends, so hopefully I can post them then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T02:22:06-07:00","id":1215713,"title":"","content":"I've made more updates to the Totem section to better reflect my ephemeral being house rules. Expect the rules themselves to appear on my hub later once I make the final touches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T21:15:23-07:00","id":1444293,"title":"","content":"So. After reading Night Horrors: Shunned By the Moon, I think I'm going to be revisiting and expanding on this homebrew Lodge of mine to integrate some/most/all of the new fluff in that book. Stay tuned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:34:36-07:00","id":1445293,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Of All Tribes and None</u></b><br /> As it is an open secret that their members are split between the Forsaken and Pure in addition to including Ghost Wolves, the Unmarked are often treated with suspicion at best by other Uratha. Outsiders think it would be a matter of time before their enemies and rivals use the lodge against them. While this has indeed happened, there are few recorded instances of it. None were done without severe repercussions from the Eaters of Names.<br /> <br /> The lodge takes measures to avoid being in the crossfire whenever Forsaken and Pure clash. While its services are called upon by both divisions of the People, the price they demand is high. Those who seek the aid of the Nameless Wolves must pay in debts, favors, and knowledge. Of the last, they prize the knowledge of names the most.<br /> <br /> As knowing one's true name allows the lodge to gain power over them, petitioners will only offer theirs if their request is one that cannot afford refusal. Instead, they either bargain with knowledge which might benefit the lodge or agree to render favors for them in pursuit of their own agenda. Whatever the agreement is in exchange for Unmarked aid, neither failure nor refusal to honor it is taken lightly.<br /> <br /> The Wolf must Hunt.<br /> <br /> And the lodge will have its due.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Hunting Grounds</u></b><ul><li>In the packless culture of Tokyo, the Nanashi form one of the city's major packs. While the Tazei ni Buzei seek to rally their fellow Uratha and 36Love consolidates its hold on mass media, they direct their energy toward more spiritual matters. More than a few local Unmarked take point in safeguarding a number of the city's shrines, and they are equally invested in the maintenance of Shinjuku Gyoen as a shared meeting place. The Nanashi are also the werewolves most involved in matters on the local Awakened and the so-called Voyagers.</li> <li>With the threat of the Warden hanging over their kind, Dubai's Nameless Wolves broker unlikely alliances to survive. They work with the Agency on a regular basis, invoking their spirit magic in tandem with their allies' occult pacts to conceal themselves as they conduct their shadow war. Such extensive collaboration has led to many secrets exchanged between the two groups. Whether or not these same secrets will be their undoing remains to be seen, however.</li> <li>The Eaters of Names stalk the shadows of Paris in their hunting of the city's spirit cults. Whether it's a tyrant's congregation or a cabal of high sorcerers, they tirelessly ferret out their secrets and weaknesses before purging them so savagely that not even their names remain. Even the Fire-Touched cults are not spared; this branch of the lodge has barred <i>Anshega</i> from its ranks since its Pure adherents turned on them.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-23-2021, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https: